From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:58:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the console's on-screen keyboard types into the game
 (Wine patch 0922)

A click of the touchpad with two fingers opens the console's keyboard over
the game (PC5's title code). Its text, once accepted, goes to Wine as input
of a new kind, one UTF-16 unit each, which the PS5 driver types as Windows
types a character from an input method (Wine patch 0922: KEYEVENTF_UNICODE,
so the game gets WM_CHAR). The click is hidden from the game, from its
press to its release.
---
